In <10783@phoenix.Princeton.EDU> jhh@pupthy.PRINCETON.EDU (Jim Horne) writes:
>Dan Quayle-V has ascended to demigoddess-hood.
>It took a blessed +8 broadsword named Stormbringer (I had about 10 of
>this type), -39 armor class, and two amulets of life preservation.  I
>couldn't have done it without polymorphing huge stacks of toys, mostly
>of the "(" type and getting lots of magic lamps. It took a long time.

Stendhal-P almost did it.  He had -45 AC, +6 Excalibur (is Stormbringer
better?), 3 amulets of lifesaving, and all imaginable accessories & innates
(although only 54 HP).  He, also, acquired these through polymorphing.  (Is it
possible to win without?  I don't think so.)  Don't know what a magic lamp is;
I got my Excalibur by dipping (set your luck to 10 before you try this at
home!)).  The priest has a great advantage in that he can work blessed scrolls
more reliably; he got his AC through this, and also genocided just about
everything dangerous in the dungeon this way.  Teleported to level 45, and
used a binary search to find the Wiz.  (Try looking at a mirror when blind.)
The Wizard was not especially dangerous because of that armor class, and gray
dragon scale mail (magic resistant); but every time he got low on hit points,
he would teleport.  He finally solved this problem himself by summoning a
cockatrice (probably the most dangerous monster left in the dungeon at this
point.)  I killed the beast, picked it up, and bashed him with the corpse.  He
died.  (Since him summoning up one of these things is not very likely, you
might want to save a charge on your wand of wishing for this.)  So far,
everything was great.  Stendhal ascended to the stronghold level, and was
faced with a problem: he had no way of crossing the trapdoors in the castle,
because his ring of levitation had become cursed, and he didn't want to put it
on.  At this point, Stendhal forsook his usual reason, and tried to polymorph
himself into a giant bat and fly across.  Unfortunately, he did not know two things:

1) Polymorphing into a giant bat destroys body armor.
2) Giant bats have a very low carrying capacity.

He was staring at the shreds and scales of his +6 Hawaiian shirt, +4 gray
dragon scale mail, and +6 cloak of protection, collapsed on the ground, when
the Wizard counterattacked.  Stendhal quickly returned to human form, but did
not have armor or weapons on, and so had to retreat - into one of the
trapdoors.  Unfortunately, the wizard followed him.  However, he managed
to get suited up while losing only one amulet of lifesaving, and probably
could have killed the Wizard, as he still had AC -29; but he tried to
polymorph into a demilich.  This was when he discovered that it is impossible
to polymorph into something you have genocided.  He became a new man.  It
seemed, though, that the new man did not have the old one's fire resistance:

"The flames of Hell burn you to a crisp.  The flames of Hell burn you to a crisp
--More--

This looped infinitely.  I had to kill the program from another shell, &
didn't even get to make the high score list.  (I was running Patchlevel 4).

Questions:

1) Is this bug fixed?  When will it be fixed?

2) Is Stormbringer better than Excalibur?

3) What is a magic lamp, and how do I use it?

4) Has anybody ever won 3.0 without polymorphing?  This is unbelievably tedious.

5) Why?

